      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a\\cdot (2b\\times (-4)c) & =-128 \\\\ 4\\cdot 2\\cdot (-4)\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =-128 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring out the constants in the requested product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot ((-4)c\\times 3a) & =(-4)\\cdot 3[b\\cdot (c\\times a)] \\\\ & =(-4)\\cdot 3\\cdot 4 \\\\ & =-48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
