      ":question/id": "7ea92732-1301-5bdf-ab1e-e800213b2b09",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Find $a\\cdot (3c\\times 4b)$, if $2a\\cdot (2b\\times 3c)=108.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a\\cdot (2b\\times 3c) & =108 \\\\ 2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =108 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $b$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (c\\times b) & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring out the constants in the requested product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (3c\\times 4b) & =3\\cdot 4[a\\cdot (c\\times b)] \\\\ & =3\\cdot 4\\cdot (-9) \\\\ & =-108.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
